<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's Telecel boosts profit 199 pct.</title>
<headline>Portugal's Telecel boosts profit 199 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending Dec 31</p>
<p>(In billions of escudos unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				7.3   vs   2.4</p>
<p>    Turnover				 58.8   vs  32.4</p>
<p>    Operating costs			45.5   vs  28.4</p>
<p>    Amortisation and depreciation     6.2   vs   4.5</p>
<p>    Operating cashflow		   19.6   vs   8.2</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			 11.6   (up 376 percent)</p>
<p>    Investment			     14.8   (up 31 percent)</p>
<p>Note - Telecel-Comunicacoes Pessoais is full company name.  </p>
<p>The company said that the number of clients rose 87 percent in the year to 331,388.</p>
<p>The average monthly income per client fell four percent to 17,233 escudos reflecting new tarifs aimed at the private consumer market, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;Telecel is beginning to give its shareholders the results that we predicted when we entered the sector,&quot; chairman Antonio Carrapatoso said.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
